sections.body:
Skip, or answer on instinct and move on, when:

- after 20 seconds you have not worked out which data you need;
- the question requires 4 or more steps and you are behind on the checkpoint;
- you have already spent twice the budget.

In most of these tests wrong answers do not cost points: always read the instructions, but in general **never leave an answer blank**. If you have to guess, do it in a reasoned way:

- eliminate the options with the wrong sign or order of magnitude;
- among the remaining ones, choose the one consistent with your estimate;
- if the test allows you to go back, flag the question and return to it at the end only if you have time left.
